        "original_id": "648f0d18-8f74-5836-b3d2-488865a8b286",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Bracco Italiano, St. John's water dog\n- Places: Italy, Newfoundland\n- Roles: gun dog\n- Concepts: landrace, extinction\n\nFacts:\n- The Bracco Italiano is a breed of dog developed in Italy as a versatile gun dog.\n- The St. John's water dog was a landrace of domestic dog from Newfoundland and was also known as the St. John’s dog or the lesser Newfoundland.\n- The number of St. John's water dogs began declining by the start of the 20th century.\n- The St. John's water dog was extinct by the early 1980s.",
